From: Chao Yu <chao@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:35:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs: fix to pass folio->index to
 f2fs_sanity_check_node_footer()
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.51
Git-commit: 7e188e9f9437ab47c3237d609f1b26348d6fea1a

commit 7e188e9f9437ab47c3237d609f1b26348d6fea1a upstream.

Otherwise in f2fs_sanity_check_node_footer(), it will check the
same nid incorrectly.

Cc: stable@kernel.org
Fixes: 0a736109c9d2 ("f2fs: fix to do sanity check on node footer in __write_node_folio()")
Signed-off-by: Chao Yu <chao@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jaegeuk Kim <jaegeuk@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 fs/f2fs/node.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/f2fs/node.c b/fs/f2fs/node.c
index 95a0df6396c0..823b78c4aa5b 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/node.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/node.c
@@ -1767,7 +1767,7 @@ static bool __write_node_folio(struct folio *folio, bool atomic, bool do_fsync,
 	/* get old block addr of this node page */
 	nid = nid_of_node(folio);
 
-	if (f2fs_sanity_check_node_footer(sbi, folio, nid,
+	if (f2fs_sanity_check_node_footer(sbi, folio, folio->index,
 					NODE_TYPE_REGULAR, false)) {
 		f2fs_handle_critical_error(sbi, STOP_CP_REASON_CORRUPTED_NID);
 		goto redirty_out;
-- 
2.53.0

